From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VeilSilence <BoneFeaR@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:47:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: make MemoryMapper worker refcount PORT_ATOMIC

MemoryMapperWorkerParams::numRefs is incremented and decremented with
portAtomicIncrementU32()/portAtomicDecrementU32(), but the field is a
plain NvU32.

With the C11 atomics backend (NVPORT_HAS_C11_ATOMICS=1, which GCC and
clang use for kernel C builds), those macros expand to
atomic_fetch_add_explicit()/atomic_fetch_sub_explicit() and require a
pointer to an _Atomic type.  clang rejects the build:

  src/kernel/gpu/mem_mgr/mem_mapper.c:197:9: error: address argument to
  atomic operation must be a pointer to _Atomic type ('NvU32 *' invalid)
  src/kernel/gpu/mem_mgr/mem_mapper.c:374:5: ...
  src/kernel/gpu/mem_mgr/mem_mapper.c:596:5: ...

Use PORT_ATOMIC, the nvport portability annotation already used by other
generated headers (for example g_gpu_mgr_nvoc.h), so the C11 backend gets
_Atomic and the builtins backends get volatile.

Build-tested with clang 23 against Linux 7.3; the changed construct also
compiles with GCC 16.2.0 under -std=gnu11.

Fixes: 5167bd2e387c ("nvidia: fix MemoryMapper worker refcount race and waiter callback UAF")
---
 src/nvidia/generated/g_mem_mapper_nvoc.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/generated/g_mem_mapper_nvoc.h b/src/nvidia/generated/g_mem_mapper_nvoc.h
index eb013c24..0dfaad77 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/generated/g_mem_mapper_nvoc.h
+++ b/src/nvidia/generated/g_mem_mapper_nvoc.h
@@ -103,7 +103,7 @@ typedef struct MemoryMapper MemoryMapper;
 typedef struct
 {
     struct MemoryMapper *pMemoryMapper;
-    NvU32         numRefs;
+    PORT_ATOMIC NvU32 numRefs;
     PORT_RWLOCK  *pLock;
     struct OBJGPU *pGpu;
     NVOS10_EVENT_KERNEL_CALLBACK_EX semaphoreCallback;
